{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 47, :comments ["<b>The entire congregation of Israel.</b> All those of obligation-age are required to make the Pesach. When I searched in the Torah, I found that the twenty-three karet punishments stated in the Torah are all of them in negative commandments, but in positive commandments I found only the Pesach alone and circumcision. Perhaps this is so because the Exodus from Egypt carries an obligation to mention it, and there is no mention greater than eating the Pesach at its appointed time, and at the beginning of the Ten Commandments He said: who brought you out of the land of Egypt (below 20:2)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:33:58.414714001Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}